# Do not break existing features

This is a hard global rule. New work is not allowed to rewrite, hide, or change behaviour of a screen the user did not ask to change.

## Before editing

1. Name the route, button, table/RPC, and role the ticket needs.
2. Open only those files. Do not "tidy" sibling pages, shared CSS, chrome, or widgets as a side effect.
3. If a shared file must change (`globals.css`, `AppShell`, usage meter), keep every existing class and control working for pages you are not building.

## Forbidden without an explicit user ask

- Restyling or relaying out Home, Analyse, Report, Library, Billing, or Admin as a side effect of another ticket
- Removing, merging, or collapsing widgets that already rendered
- Changing default open/closed, filter commit, or URL state
- Deleting a button, href, or RPC call because a new page exists
- Rewriting a saved report in place (refinements **append**; original verdict stays)

## After UI edits

The previously working surface must still show the same widgets, filters, and click paths. If you cannot keep that, stop and ask — do not ship a new layout.

## Mock lock (until product UI ships)

Canonical screens are `docs/mock-ui/Thesis.dc.html` (app) and `docs/mock-ui/Home.dc.html` (marketing). Do not invent extra nav items. Screen ids: `login`, `signup`, `reset`, `home`, `build`, `portfolio`, `clarify`, `report`, `library`, `usage`, `billing`, `admin`, `arch`.

Work only the ROADMAP **Build next** chunk. Filling `/analyse` is not a reason to restyle `/desk`.
